# Phase 4: Core Foundations & Runtime Configuration

> **Precondition:** Phase 3 gate verified (health probe is live).
> **Outputs:** env contract, i18n, theme tokens, layout shell, telemetry, global
> error boundaries.

---

## Deliverables & Tasks

- [ ] **4.1 Environment contract**
  - Author `.env.example` as the production template and `.env.development` for
    local work; document load order and categories; ignore every `.env*` except
    the committed templates.
  - **Acceptance:** `git check-ignore` ignores `.env`, `.env.local`, and
    `.env.production` while the two templates stay tracked; `pnpm build` reads
    the expected values.
  - **Negative:** no secret has a production-valid default; startup fails fast
    when a required value is missing.
  - **Drift check:** every variable referenced in code appears in both templates.
  - **Evidence:** variable count, ignored-file check
  - **Result:** —

- [ ] **4.2 Localization**
  - Configure request negotiation and routing; dictionaries in root `messages/`;
    LTR/RTL layout direction; font pairings per locale.
  - **Acceptance:** the default locale renders; switching locale changes copy and
    `dir`; build passes.
  - **Negative:** an unknown locale falls back to the default instead of 500.
  - **Evidence:** locale list, dictionary key count
  - **Result:** —

- [ ] **4.3 Theme tokens**
  - Define semantic tokens in the global stylesheet (light + dark), a provider
    with system preference and persistence, and a toggle.
  - **Acceptance:** toggling changes tokens, persists on reload, and respects
    `prefers-color-scheme` on first visit.
  - **Negative:** no raw palette class or arbitrary value is used in components;
    the design-system lint passes.
  - **Evidence:** token count, contrast check result
  - **Result:** —

- [ ] **4.4 Layout shell**
  - Root layout with locale-aware `lang`/`dir` and fonts; providers; header and
    footer; zero-CLS font loading.
  - **Acceptance:** every page renders inside the shell; CLS is 0 in a local
    Lighthouse/Playwright run.
  - **Negative:** the shell renders without a provider crash when telemetry is
    disabled.
  - **Evidence:** CLS value, viewport checks
  - **Result:** —

- [ ] **4.5 Telemetry (pack: opentelemetry)**
  - Dependencies `@vercel/otel` + `@opentelemetry/api`, root `src/`-aware
    `instrumentation.ts`, error context on `onRequestError`, and `OTEL_*` keys in
    both env templates.
  - **Acceptance:** a request produces a span at the mock collector
    (`POST /v1/traces` → 200, > 0 bytes); `pnpm exec tsc --noEmit` → 0.
  - **Negative (mandatory):** `OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=true` logs the skip line and
    exports **0** traces; `OTEL_SDK_DISABLED=false` must still export (the
    `@vercel/otel` truthiness bug).
  - **Evidence:** collector log, span name, kill-switch run
  - **Result:** —
  - _If the pack is disabled: mark `Skipped on purpose` with a revisit trigger._


- [ ] **4.6 Global error boundaries**
  - Root `global-error.tsx`, localized `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`, and the
    authorization pages the app needs (401/403).
  - **Acceptance:** a thrown error renders the boundary with a working reset; an
    unknown route renders the not-found page.
  - **Negative:** error pages leak no stack trace or secret in production mode.
  - **Evidence:** screenshots or route checks
  - **Result:** —

---

**Phase 4 gate:** a page can render inside the shell in both directions, with a
persisted theme, localized copy, working boundaries, a live health probe, and
traces proven active **and** silenced by the kill switch (or the OTel pack marked
skipped with a revisit trigger).

